    "q-143515": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143515",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "| $x$ | $-8$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n\nLet ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{60}$ be a random sample of size $n=60$ from a population with the probability mass function given above. Find an approximation for the probability that the sample mean is less than $-4.5.$\n\n*Note: $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ The central limit theorem (or CLT) states that for sufficiently large $n,$ the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ can be approximated as \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case:\n\n- the sample size is \n\n$$\nn=60,\n$$\n\n- the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}f({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-8)\\cdot 0.3+(-4)\\cdot 0.3+(-2)\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.1 \\\\  & =-2.4-1.2-0.6+0.2 \\\\  & =-4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =((-8)^{2}\\cdot 0.3+(-4)^{2}\\cdot 0.3+(-2)^{2}\\cdot 0.3+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.1)-(-4)^{2} \\\\  & =(19.2+4.8+1.2+0.4)-16 \\\\  & =9.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the CLT, we have that the distribution of the sample mean can be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}) \\\\  & ∼N\\,(-4,\\frac{9.6}{60}) \\\\  & ∼N(-4,0.16).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find $P(\\overset{―}{X}<-4.5).$ So, we convert $\\overset{―}{X}$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}<-4.5) & ≈P(Z<\\frac{-4.5-(-4)}{\\sqrt{0.16}}) \\\\  & =P(Z<-1.25) \\\\  & =Φ(-1.25).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(\\overset{―}{X}<-4.5)=Φ(-1.25).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-143515-a",
